          "derivation": "Two of the four items are straight Avestan and confirmed; two are not. (a) xʳasta- (Nourai's 'xvâsto') 'made savoury by cooking, cooked' is Pokorny's 'Avestan xʳasto „durch Kochen (schmackhaft) gemacht“ = Old Indic svādita-'; Bartholomae AiW col. 300 has the privative a-xʳasta- 'ungekocht' (N 57). It is the exact homonym of the 'threshed' participle of the previous chart, from a different root. (b) xʳandra-kara- 'doing what is pleasing, compliant' is Avestan and nasalised (*su̯ad-n-ro-), as Pokorny and Walde-Pokorny II 517 say; Nourai's cross-reference to root Kwer for the second member (-kara- 'making') is correct. (c) 'xvand “sweet taste”' is NOT Avestan: both Pokorny ('afgh. xʳand „Wohlgeschmack, pleasure“') and Walde-Pokorny and Cheung ('Pash. xwand (m.) “taste, pleasure”') label it Pashto/Afghan; Nourai has silently promoted it into the Avestan box. (d) 'xwâs, xwâd “to desire”' is no attested Avestan verb either: it is Abolghasemi's reconstructed Old Iranian root *xwād- with its pre-dental allomorph xwās-, posited precisely to yield MP xwāst/xwāh (FFD 51), and Nourai's second cited reference is that page.",
