          "derivation": "New Persian خواستن, classically xʷāstan, is the direct continuation of MP xwāstan with no change beyond the loss of the labial glide of xʷ- (the so-called vāv-e ma'dūla, still written خوا- but silent from about the 16th-17th c., hence modern xāstan); the present stem خواه xāh continues MP xwāh-. The extras of the box are the regular derivatives: خواست (past stem used as a noun, 'will'), خواستار (agent in -ār, MP xwāstār), خواهش (verbal noun in -išn, MP xwāhišn), خواه (present stem as an independent word); to these Mo'in's footnote at Borhan 783 adds خواسته 'property' = MP xwāstag. The step from MP to NP is beyond doubt; what remains 'plausible' rather than 'confirmed' is only the further step back to the 'sweet' root (see node 2): Horn 110, Hübschmann §92 and Aryanpur take it, Nyberg's *hvāz- and Wiktionary's Proto-Iranian *xwaz- ('of uncertain origin, perhaps ultimately from PIE *sweh₂d-') do not. Note also that the Wiktionary page's only bibliographical reference for this family is Nourai 2011 p. 459 — this very page — so it is no independent witness.",
